{{Quote|Taika's approach to Star Wars will be fresh, unexpected, and&hellip;unique. His enormous talent and sense of humor will ensure that audiences are in for an unforgettable ride.|Kathleen Kennedy|<ref name="Investor SW.com">{{SW|url=news/future-lucasfilm-projects-revealed|text=Future Lucasfilm Projects Revealed}}</ref>}}
A '''''[[Star Wars]]'' film''' written and directed by [[Taika Waititi]] is currently being developed at [[Lucasfilm]]. The project was officially announced on [[May 4]], [[2020]].

==Development==
===Initial announcement===
In [[January]] [[2020]], [[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']] revealed that [[Taika Waititi]] was approached to work on a ''[[Star Wars]]'' movie.<ref>{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/taika-waititi-courted-star-wars-movie-1269996|text=Taika Waititi courted for Star Wars Movie|author=Borys Kit; Kim Masters|date=2020-01-16|work=[[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']]|archivedate=20210602223953}}</ref> The project was officially announced on [[May 4]] on [[StarWars.com]], confirming Waititi's involvement and the addition of [[Krysty Wilson-Cairns]] as a co-writer.<ref name="Announcement" />

[[File:TaikaPromoArt.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Promotional art shown during the December 2020 Disney investor's call.]]
During a [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] investor's broadcast in [[December]] 2020, [[Lucasfilm]] President [[Kathleen Kennedy]] confirmed that Waititi was already at work on the film's script. A ''Star Wars'' logo designed in Waititi's signature style was shown during the film's portion of the announcement, along with art featuring a diamond-shaped object floating in space.<ref name="Investor 2020 Showcase">{{DisneyCompany|url=disney-investor-day-2020|text=Disney Investor Day 2020}}</ref> On [[November 8]], [[2021]], in an interview with [[Wikipedia:Wired UK|''Wired UK'']], Waititi revealed that the film's script was still in very early stages, but that "we've got a story. I'm really excited by it because it feels very me."<ref name="Wired Interview">{{WebCite|url=https://www.wired.co.uk/article/taika-waititi-free-guy|text=Taika Waititi talks ''Free Guy'', ''Star Wars'' and ''Thor''|date=2021-11-08|work=[[Wikipedia:Wired UK|''Wired UK'']]|archivedate=20230830154006}}</ref>

===Further development===
{{Quote|Taika is still working away. He's writing the script himself and he really doesn't want to bring others into the process, and I don't blame him. He has a very, very unique voice. So I want to protect that and that's what he's doing, but we're going to make that one day.|Kathleen Kennedy|<ref name="Variety Celebration">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2023/film/news/daisy-ridley-rey-star-wars-new-movie-1235572603|text=Daisy Ridley to Reprise Role as Rey in New 'Star Wars' Film|author=Vary, Adam B.; Warmann, Amon|date=2023-04-07|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20230619200632}}</ref>}}
In [[May]] [[2022]], Kennedy revealed in a feature for [[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']] that Waititi's film was next in the pipeline of upcoming projects<ref name="Vanity Fair">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2022/05/star-wars-cover-the-rebellion-will-be-televised|text='Star Wars': The Rebellion Will Be Televised|author=Anthony Breznican|date=2022-05-17|work=[[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']]|archivedate=20220517114556}}</ref> and, in an interview with [[Wikipedia:GamesRadar+|''GamesRadar+'']], said that it was aiming for a late [[2023]] release.<ref name="GamesRadar">{{WebCite|url=https://www.gamesradar.com/star-wars-movies-kathleen-kennedy-celebration-interview|text=Kathleen Kennedy on the future of Star Wars movies: "We need to create a whole new saga"|author=Jack Shepherd|date=2022-05-26|work=[[Wikipedia:GamesRadar+|''GamesRadar+'']]|archivedate=20220527002449}}</ref> However it was not included on the 2023 Disney release schedule.<ref name="2023 Schedule">{{Twitter|ScottGustin|status/1616534374945619996|Scott Gustin|quote=Disney sent their updated movie release schedule. Looking back at the schedule released in October, I'm counting at least 7 UNTITLED movies added to 2025 and 9 UNTITLED movies added to 2026.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/a1Ery}}</ref> In an interview with [[Wikipedia:Screen Rant|''Screen Rant'']] on [[June 10]], Waititi mentioned that he was still in the writing phase for the film and that he is being very intentional to make the story feel like a ''Star Wars'' film.<ref name="ScreenRant">{{WebCite|url=https://screenrant.com/star-wars-movie-taika-waititi-script-updates|text=Taika Waititi Shares Update On His Star Wars Movie|date=2022-06-10|work=[[Wikipedia:Screen Rant|''Screen Rant'']]|archivedate=20230317132032}}</ref> Several days later, on [[June 14]], Waititi mentioned how, in his film, he wanted "to take something new and create some new characters and just expand the [''Star Wars''] world."<ref name="GamesRadar 2">{{WebCite|url=https://www.gamesradar.com/taika-waititi-star-wars-movie-new-characters|text=Taika Waititi talks his Star Wars movie: "I would like to take something new and create some new characters"|author=Molly Edwards|date=2022-06-14|work=[[Wikipedia:GamesRadar+|''GamesRadar+'']]|archivedate=20231117143754}}</ref> On [[June 27]], after rumors arose that his movie would begin to film shortly, Taika Waititi spoke out saying that his project would not enter production in 2022, and that he would be writing through the end of the year.<ref name="The Wrap">{{WebCite|url=https://www.thewrap.com/taika-waititi-star-wars-movie-filming-update-2023|text=Taika Waititi's 'Star Wars' Movie Won't Shoot This Year|author=Drew Taylor|date=2022-06-27|work=[[Wikipedia:The Wrap|''The Wrap'']]|archivedate=20230830154052}}</ref> On [[June 29]], Waititi stated in an interview that the final script that he submits to Lucasfilm would determine when it will be produced, or whether or not it will be produced at all.<ref name="NYT">{{WebCite|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/29/movies/taika-waititi-thor-love-and-thunder.html|text=What Makes Taika Waititi Run and Run and Run?|author=Dave Itzkoff|date=2022-06-29|work=[[Wikipedia:The New York Times|''The New York Times'']]|archivedate=20231029114858}}</ref> 

On [[March 7]], [[2023]], [[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']] reported that Waititi's film was still in development, and that he would possibly have an acting role in the project as well.<ref name="Variety Shakeup">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2023/film/news/star-wars-kevin-feige-patty-jenkins-movies-shelved-1235545774|text='Star Wars' Shakeup: Kevin Feige and Patty Jenkins Movies Shelved, Taika Waititi Looking to Star in His Own Film (EXCLUSIVE)|author=Adam B. Vary|date=2023-03-07|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20231114192341}}</ref> On [[April 7]], in an interview at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]], Kathleen Kennedy confirmed that Waititi was now writing the script on his own, indictating the departure of Krysty Wilson-Cairns from the project. Furthermore, she mentioned how she wants to be protective of Waititi's distinct voice in the project.<ref name="Variety Celebration" /> On [[May 10]], Waititi mentioned in an interview that he had several acts written, but was struggling in finalizing the middle act of the film, as he did not want it to feel too derivative of other ''Star Wars'' material.<ref name="THR May">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/taika-waititi-next-goal-wins-reservation-dogs-representation-1235503336|text=Taika Waititi: "Am I Allowed to Laugh at This?"|author=Rebecca Keegan|date=2023-05-31|work=[[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']]|archivedate=20230926055333}}</ref>

In [[November]] [[2024]], Waititi was asked on the ''The Playlist''{{'s}} ''Bingeworthy'' podcast about the development status of his ''Star Wars'' film, his planned ''[[Wikipedia:Flash Gordon|Flash Gordon]]'' reboot, and a live-action adaptation of [[Wikipedia:Akira (1988 film)|''Akira'']]. He vaguely said that they are still planned but are not currently in active development.<ref name="Playlist">{{WebCite|url=https://theplaylist.net/interior-chinatown-taika-waititi-showrunner-charles-yu-discuss-their-surreal-comedy-series-background-characters-star-wars-more-bingeworthy-podcast-20241121|text=‘Interior Chinatown’: Taika Waititi & Showrunner Charles Yu Discuss Their Surreal Comedy Series, Background Characters, ‘Star Wars’ & More|author=Mike DeAngelo|date=2024-11-21|work=[https://theplaylist.net ''The Playlist'']|archivedate=20241124070459}}</ref> On [[February 27]], [[2025]], Lucasfilm president [[Kathleen Kennedy]] revealed to Deadline that she was waiting for another script by Waititi and a different writer. A first act was also seen by Kennedy, which she enjoyed.<ref name="KK Q&A">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2025/02/kathleen-kennedy-clarifies-lucasfilm-exit-star-wars-future-1236304421|text=Kathleen Kennedy Speaks On Her Lucasfilm Plans — She Is Not Soon Retiring — & The Films That Will Keep Her In 'Star Wars' Orbit For Years To Come|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20250228034942}}</ref>

In an interview with ''[[Wikipedia:Screenrant|Screenrant]]'' at [[Celebration Japan (2025)|Celebration Japan]] on [[April 18]], Kennedy restated that the film was still in development and taking its time and also revealed that [[Tony McNamara]] was hired as a new writer.<ref name="Namara" /> In January [[2026]], as she announced her retirement, Kennedy described the film as "still somewhat alive" and that its fate would be in the hands of her successors, [[Dave Filoni]] and [[Lynwen Brennan]]. She called his script "hilarious and great."<ref name="Deadline Kennedy">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2026/01/kathleen-kennedy-exit-interview-1236665253/|text=A Shift In The Force For Lucasfilm’s Kathleen Kennedy: The Exit Interview|author=Mike Flemming Jr.|date=2026-01-15|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20260115233219}}</ref>

